+            # OPAQUE `Some` ARM (relaunch #16). A CLASS-shaped arm with no record
+            # type_decl used to degrade to `Any` and be DROPPED — on the ground that its
+            # payload would int-erase, "exactly the kind of facade this capability exists
+            # to remove". Measured, the DROP is the worse of the two: it collapses the
+            # union to `Arm_<i>_None` ALONE, a type with exactly ONE inhabitant, so every
+            # `x is None` guard on such a value lowers to a literal `true` (lesson (bl))
+            # and the model CLAIMS the value is always absent — a positive FALSE statement
+            # (lesson (ca)). An int-erased `Some` arm claims strictly LESS: the PRESENCE is
+            # modelled faithfully and only the payload is opaque. Module6 resolves an
+            # unknown payload tag to the int default, so no Module6 change is needed and
+            # each distinct class keeps its own arm signature.
+            # Gated on a CLASS-SHAPED name (leading capital, not a typing alias) so a
+            # builtin or an alias still takes the paths above.
+            if (elt.id[:1].isupper()
+                    and elt.id not in ("Any", "Optional", "Union", "List", "Dict", "Set",
+                                       "FrozenSet", "Tuple", "Type", "Callable",
+                                       "Sequence", "Mapping", "Iterable", "Iterator",
+                                       "Literal", "Final", "ClassVar", "NoReturn",
+                                       "Text", "AnyStr", "ByteArray", "Bytes")):
